What Is the Data Center Interconnect Market?
Data center interconnect (DCI) solutions connect geographically separated data centers through high-bandwidth optical transmission systems, coherent pluggable optics, network switches, and supporting software. These technologies enable organizations to exchange data between facilities while maintaining network performance, reliability, and operational continuity.

Growing cloud infrastructure, distributed artificial intelligence workloads, and demand for low-latency connectivity are increasing the importance of DCI solutions. Hyperscale cloud providers, colocation operators, and enterprise networks are investing in higher-capacity optical infrastructure to support expanding data traffic.

Key Market Drivers
Increasing Bandwidth Demand from AI Workloads
Distributed AI model training requires large volumes of data to move between physically separate computing facilities. This is increasing demand for high-capacity optical links and advanced transmission technologies that can support demanding bandwidth requirements.

Adoption of Coherent Optical Technologies
Coherent pluggable optics are enabling higher transmission capacity while improving the utilization of existing fiber infrastructure. The development of 400G and 800G technologies is supporting the evolution of modern interconnect networks.

Expansion of Hyperscale and Colocation Infrastructure
Cloud providers and colocation operators are expanding data center footprints across metropolitan and regional markets. Connecting these facilities requires reliable optical transport systems capable of supporting high-speed data exchange and network resilience.

