Market Challenges
High implementation and qualification costs can complicate DCI deployments. Network operators must evaluate optical equipment, fiber availability, integration requirements, and long-term maintenance costs before committing to infrastructure upgrades.

Technical compatibility between existing network equipment and newer coherent transmission platforms can also increase deployment complexity. Operators must balance capacity requirements with service continuity and infrastructure investment.

Market Restraints
Limited supplier readiness and downstream installation capabilities can delay deployment. Specialized equipment, skilled technical personnel, and network qualification processes may extend implementation timelines.

Regulatory and technical uncertainty across markets can also affect investment decisions, particularly where infrastructure projects depend on permits, fiber access, and cross-border connectivity arrangements.

